data.content:
**No Thread.Abort migration is needed here.**

Your code only uses `Thread.Start()`, `Thread.Join()`, and `Thread.Sleep()` — none of which are affected by the Thread.Abort removal in .NET 6+. These APIs work identically in modern .NET, and this code will compile and run correctly as-is on .NET 8.

---

**Optional modernization (unrelated to Thread.Abort):** You could replace the manual thread management with `Parallel.ForEach` or `Task.Run` for cleaner code and better thread-pool utilization:

```csharp
public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    Parallel.ForEach(items, item => Process(item));
}
```

Or with tasks:

```csharp
public async Task RunBatchAsync(List<WorkItem> items)
{
    await Task.WhenAll(items.Select(item => Task.Run(() => Process(item))));
}
```

These are **optional improvements** — your existing code is fully functional on .NET 8 without changes.
